1
00:00:00,290 --> 00:00:02,320
This week I changed what I'm entering.

2
00:00:02,470 --> 00:00:04,780
Confide stays where it was submitted first.

3
00:00:04,830 --> 00:00:08,860
For this fair, I moved to the Tempo track,
where my Reth and Revm work fits.

4
00:00:08,980 --> 00:00:10,490
The product is Sworn.

5
00:00:10,880 --> 00:00:15,720
On MPP, if a paid answer is wrong,
a refund is the server's choice.

6
00:00:16,060 --> 00:00:20,640
Sworn makes the server reserve
its own bond behind each answer.

7
00:00:21,140 --> 00:00:23,460
Here a server says the payment lands;

8
00:00:23,590 --> 00:00:26,160
Tempo's receive policy diverts it.

9
00:00:26,610 --> 00:00:29,930
A zero-knowledge proof of Tempo's own EVM catches it,

10
00:00:30,100 --> 00:00:32,020
and the bond pays the agent —

11
00:00:32,280 --> 00:00:34,270
this transaction, on Moderato.

12
00:00:34,660 --> 00:00:35,540
What I learned:

13
00:00:35,590 --> 00:00:40,020
our first full run said "blocked",
but the transfer had simply run out of gas —

14
00:00:40,110 --> 00:00:43,730
Tempo prices storage about eleven times Ethereum.

15
00:00:44,290 --> 00:00:45,190
The test caught it.

16
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:47,830
Next: the demo and the submission.
